","r":"dish/bagel","n":"Bagel","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#a99fb5","intro":[["A bagel is a bread roll originating in the Jewish communities of Poland. Bagels are traditionally made from yeasted wheat dough that is shaped by hand into a torus or ring, briefly boiled in water, and then baked. The result is a dense, chewy, doughy interior with a browned and sometimes crisp exterior."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bagel"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagel"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine"],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Tori Avey: Jewish Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"toriavey.com","note":"Tori Avey's Jewish recipe index, often paired with notes on each dish's history.","url":"https://toriavey.com/jewish-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"The Nosher (My Jewish Learning)","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"myjewishlearning.com","note":"Recipe section of the nonprofit My Jewish Learning, covering Ashkenazi, Sephardi and Mizrahi home cooking and holiday food.","url":"https://www.myjewishlearning.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"},{"name":"Polonist","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polonist.com","note":"Polish recipes and food culture from a Polish-born writer living abroad.","url":"https://www.polonist.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Polish Your Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polishyourkitchen.com","note":"Long-running blog of traditional Polish home recipes.","url":"https://polishyourkitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Jewish cuisine","links":[["Appetizing store","dish/appetizing-store"],["Brisket (Jewish dish)","dish/brisket-jewish-