 Rouchy) is a species of tree from the genus Prunus. Along with the peach, it is classified in the subgenus Amygdalus, distinguished from the other subgenera by corrugations on the woody shell (endocarp) surrounding the seed."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-almonds"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almonds"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine",[["Ostkaka","dish/ostkaka"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Almonds, in shell","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":3866489,"top":[["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",2034142],["Spain","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",339102],["Ashmore and Cartier Is.","cuisine/australian-cuisine",325800],["Turkey","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",179437],["Morocco","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",157906],["Iran","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",115746],["Syria","cuisine/syrian-cuisine",87733],["Italy","cuisine/italian-cuisine",75874],["Tunisia","cuisine/tunisian-cuisine",67862],["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",66800],["Algeria","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",63548],["Afghanistan","cuisine/afghan-cuisine",60679],["Portugal","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",55910],["Chile","cuisine/chilean-cuisine",47187],["Libya","cuisine/libyan-cuisine",35283]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bitter almond","ingredient/bitter-almond"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Rennet","ingredient/rennet"],["Saffron","ingredient/saffron"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/37/Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg/500px-Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Ivar Leidus","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg"}},"ingredient/sea-cucumber":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sea-cucumber","n":"Sea cucumber","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Sea cucumbers are benthic echinoderms of the class Holothuroidea that are consumed as seafood, in fresh or dried form, in various Asian and Oceanian cuisines. In some cultural contexts, they are thought to have medicinal value."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sea-cucumber"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_cucumber_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Korean Chinese cuisine","cuisine/korean-chinese-cuisine",[["Ulmyeon","dish/ulmyeon"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Agaricus bisporus","ingredient/agaricus-bisporus"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Cornstarch","ingredient/cornstarch"],["Cuttlefish","ingredient/cuttlefish"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Noodle","ingredient/noodle"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Shiitake","ingredient/shiitake"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"],["Squid as food","ingredient/squid-as-food"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/ba/Prickly_sea_cucumber_soup.jpg/500px-Prickly_sea_cucumber_soup.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Jpatokal","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prickly_sea_cucumber_soup.jpg"}},"ingredient/camassia":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/camassia","n":"Camas","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 0 dishes across 0 cuisines","intro":[["A wild bulb of Northwest meadows. ",["Coast Salish","cuisine/coast-salish-foodways"]," nations hold intertribal camas harvests that bring Elders and youth together, and ",["Nuu-chah-nulth","cuisine/nuu-chah-nulth-foodways"]," families gather the bulbs in spri